@startuml
' Figure 46.6  Level four: durability
' Reading order: top to bottom. The worker writes the step and its key
' to the log before the call; the worker dies; the resumed worker reads
' the log and sends the same key; the tool returns the first result
' instead of acting twice. From the P07 prompt and the A07a note.
!include plantuml-theme.puml
participant "Worker" as W <<ops>>
participant "Durable log" as L <<evidence>>
participant "Rebook tool" as T <<ops>>
W -> L : Step 4, key k
W -> T : Rebook, key k
W -[$FAIL]> W : Crash
W -> L : Read step 4
L -> W : Key k
W -> T : Rebook, key k
T -> W : First result
W -> L : Step 4 done
@enduml
